    <node id="Claimify">
      <data key="d2">Claimify</data>
      <data key="d3">Method</data>
      <data key="d4">An LLM-based method that identifies sentences containing factual claims and decomposes them into simple claims.</data>
      <data key="d5">To extract factual claims, we used Claimify (Metropolitansky and Larson, 2025), an LLM-based method that identifies sentences in an answer containing at least one factual claim, then decomposes these sentences into simple, self-contained factual claims.</data>
      <data key="d6">[9]</data>
      <data key="d7">["To extract factual claims, we used Claimify (Metropolitansky and Larson, 2025), an LLM-based method that identifies sentences in an answer containing at least one factual claim, then decomposes these sentences into simple, self-contained factual claims."]</data>
      <data key="d8">semantically_reviewed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Claims">
      <data key="d2">Claims</data>
      <data key="d3">Concept</data>
      <data key="d4">Verifiable facts extracted by LLMs used to validate results.</data>
      <data key="d5">LLM-extracted statements of verifiable facts, or "claims."</data>
      <data key="d6">[4]</data>
      <data key="d7">["LLM-extracted statements of verifiable facts, or \"claims.\""]</data>
      <data key="d8">semantically_reviewed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Answers">
      <data key="d2">Community Answers</data>
      <data key="d3">Concept</data>
      <data key="d4">Intermediate answers generated in parallel to address specific questions before reduction to a global answer.</data>
      <data key="d5">Given a user query, the community summaries generated in the previous step can be used to generate a final answer in a multi-stage process</data>
      <data key="d6">[6]</data>
      <data key="d7">["Given a user query, the community summaries generated in the previous step can be used to generate a final answer in a multi-stage process"]</data>
      <data key="d8">semantically_reviewed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Summaries">
      <data key="d2">Community Summaries</data>
      <data key="d3">Concept</data>
      <data key="d4">Pre-generated summaries for all groups of closely related entities used to generate partial responses.</data>
      <data key="d5">then to pre-generate community summaries for all groups of closely related entities. | Next, it partitions the graph into a hierarchy of communities of closely related entities, before using an LLM to generate community-level summaries. | The next step creates report-like summaries of each community in the community hierarchy, using a method designed to scale to very large datasets | Community summaries vs. source texts. When comparing community summaries to source texts using GraphRAG, community summaries generally provided a small but consistent improvement in answer comprehensiveness and diversity, except for root-level summaries.</data>
      <data key="d6">[1, 2, 6, 10]</data>
      <data key="d7">["then to pre-generate community summaries for all groups of closely related entities.", "Next, it partitions the graph into a hierarchy of communities of closely related entities, before using an LLM to generate community-level summaries.", "The next step creates report-like summaries of each community in the community hierarchy, using a method designed to scale to very large datasets", "Community summaries vs. source texts. When comparing community summaries to source texts using GraphRAG, community summaries generally provided a small but consistent improvement in answer comprehensiveness and diversity, except for root-level summaries."]</data>
      <data key="d8">semantically_reviewed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community detection">
      <data key="d2">Community detection</data>
      <data key="d3">Method</data>
      <data key="d4">Technique used to partition the graph index into groups of elements.</data>
      <data key="d5">Community detection (e.g., Leiden, Traag et al., 2019) is used to partition the graph index</data>
      <data key="d6">[4]</data>
      <data key="d7">["Community detection (e.g., Leiden, Traag et al., 2019) is used to partition the graph index"]</data>
      <data key="d8">semantically_reviewed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Comprehensiveness">
      <data key="d2">Comprehensiveness</data>
      <data key="d3">Metric</data>
      <data key="d4">A target criterion measuring how much detail an answer provides to cover all aspects of a question.</data>
      <data key="d5">How much detail does the answer provide to cover all aspects and details of the question? | "Since directness is effectively in opposition to comprehensiveness and diversity..." | 1. Comprehensiveness: Measured as the average number of claims extracted from the answers generated under each condition. | All Graph RAG conditions outperformed na¨ıve RAG on comprehensiveness and diversity. | the claim-based measure of comprehensiveness | Pairwise comparisons of six conditions on four metrics</data>
      <data key="d6">[7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 26]</data>
      <data key="d7">["How much detail does the answer provide to cover all aspects and details of the question?", "\"Since directness is effectively in opposition to comprehensiveness and diversity...\"", "1. Comprehensiveness: Measured as the average number of claims extracted from the answers generated under each condition.", "All Graph RAG conditions outperformed na¨ıve RAG on comprehensiveness and diversity.", "the claim-based measure of comprehensiveness", "Pairwise comparisons of six conditions on four metrics"]</data>
      <data key="d8">semantically_reviewed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directness">
      <data key="d2">Directness</data>
      <data key="d3">Metric</data>
      <data key="d4">A control criterion evaluating how specifically and clearly an answer addresses a question, focusing on concision.</data>
      <data key="d5">"Directness that answers 'How specifically and clearly does the answer address the question?'" | Pairwise comparisons of six conditions on four metrics</data>
      <data key="d6">[8, 26]</data>
      <data key="d7">["\"Directness that answers 'How specifically and clearly does the answer address the question?'\"", "Pairwise comparisons of six conditions on four metrics"]</data>
      <data key="d8">semantically_reviewed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Diversity">
      <data key="d2">Diversity</data>
      <data key="d3">Metric</data>
      <data key="d4">A target criterion measuring the variety and richness of perspectives and insights in an answer.</data>
      <data key="d5">How varied and rich is the answer in providing different perspectives and insights on the question? | "Since directness is effectively in opposition to comprehensiveness and diversity..." | 2. Diversity: Measured by clustering the claims for each answer and calculating the average number of clusters. | All Graph RAG conditions outperformed na¨ıve RAG on comprehensiveness and diversity. | the claim-based measure of diversity | Pairwise comparisons of six conditions on four metrics</data>
      <data key="d6">[7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 26]</data>
      <data key="d7">["How varied and rich is the answer in providing different perspectives and insights on the question?", "\"Since directness is effectively in opposition to comprehensiveness and diversity...\"", "2. Diversity: Measured by clustering the claims for each answer and calculating the average number of clusters.", "All Graph RAG conditions outperformed na¨ıve RAG on comprehensiveness and diversity.", "the claim-based measure of diversity", "Pairwise comparisons of six conditions on four metrics"]</data>
      <data key="d8">semantically_reviewed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Empowerment">
      <data key="d2">Empowerment</data>
      <data key="d3">Metric</data>
      <data key="d4">A target criterion measuring how well an answer helps the reader understand and make informed judgments.</data>
      <data key="d5">How well does the answer help the reader understand and make informed judgments about the topic? | Pairwise comparisons of six conditions on four metrics</data>
      <data key="d6">[7, 26]</data>
      <data key="d7">["How well does the answer help the reader understand and make informed judgments about the topic?", "Pairwise comparisons of six conditions on four metrics"]</data>
