      <data key="d3">Method</data>
      <data key="d4">An approach to using LLMs to answer queries based on data that is too large to contain in a language model's context window.</data>
      <data key="d5">Retrieval augmented generation (RAG) is an established approach to using LLMs to answer queries based on data that is too large to contain in a language model's context window | RAG generally refers to any system where a user query is used to retrieve relevant information from external data sources, whereupon this information is incorporated into the generation of a response to the query by an LLM (or other generative AI model, such as a multi-media model).</data>
